  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "For years, your mortgage payment mostly feeds the bank. There's a specific turning point when it finally starts feeding the house.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "home",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "coin"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "When it starts",
            "paying the house."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Early on, almost every dollar goes to interest, with just a sliver chipping at what you owe.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "mostly interest",
          "label": "in the early years",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The amortization schedule front-loads the interest on purpose.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-amort",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · amortization"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Then, somewhere around the halfway mark of a thirty-year loan, the balance flips.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "~year 18",
          "label": "the turning point",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "After that, more of each payment builds your home equity.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-homeequity",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · home equity"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "From there on, most of each payment finally goes toward principal, the part you keep.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Now it's yours",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Refinancing can reset that clock, for better or worse.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-refi",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · refinancing"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "On a three hundred thousand dollar mortgage at seven percent, you repay around seven hundred thousand total.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "$700K",
          "label": "total repaid on a $300K loan",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Until that flip happens, you are really just renting money from the bank.",
